From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P80 builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Teclast P80: no desktop windowing on the low-RAM tablet

LineageOS 24.0 sets config_isDesktopModeSupported in its common overlay
and config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops for tablets. The P80 keeps the
stock ro.config.low_ram=true, so ActivityTaskManager reports no
multi-window and no freeform support, while WMShell's DesktopModeStatus
only looks at these resources: SystemUI's wmshell.main thread throws
"Can't create root task for unsupported windowingMode=5" from
DesktopDisplayEventHandler.createDefaultDesksIfNeeded and SystemUI
crash-loops, leaving the keyguard and the setup wizard undrawn.
---
diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -46,6 +46,14 @@
          default to this value; Settings lists color correction under "Experimental". -->
     <bool name="config_setColorTransformAccelerated">false</bool>
 
+    <!-- Teclast P80: no desktop windowing. LineageOS enables it for every device and lets
+         tablets host desktops, but ro.config.low_ram makes the window manager turn off
+         multi-window and so freeform windows, and SystemUI's shell then crashes in a loop
+         creating the default desk ("Can't create root task for unsupported windowingMode=5"),
+         which leaves the keyguard and the setup wizard undrawn. -->
+    <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">false</bool>
+    <bool name="config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops">false</bool>
+
     <bool name="config_supportAudioSourceUnprocessed">true</bool>
 
     <string-array name="config_packagesExemptFromSuspension" translatable="false">
-- 
